<title>USA: Galileo Int'l overallotment exercised.</title>
<headline>Galileo Int'l overallotment exercised.</headline>
<dateline>ROSEMONT, Ill. 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Galileo International Inc said Friday  that Morgan Stanley Dean Witter, lead underwriter for its initial  public offering, has exercised an over allotment option of 4,799,700  shares granted by the company.</p>
<p>Galileo allows travel agencies to access schedule and fare information,  book reservations and issue tickets for 525 airlines.</p>
<p>Galileo said it will use proceeds of $100 million to repay debt.</p>
<p>As a result of the exercise of the over-allotment, Galileo's total  offering is about $900 million.</p>
<p>		((Chicago newsdesk 312 408 8787))</p>
